ly aggressive with little equity and could be exploited.\n\nFolding (-1) is too passive — you still have 8 outs to the nuts (the straight), and folding now gives up equity.\n\nChecking (0) allows you to see the river for free and evaluate whether to bluff or call if bet into.\n\nReason:  \nChecking is optimal because it’s low-risk, maintains your equity, and lets you realize your draw on the river. Given your opponent has shown passivity by checking twice, they likely don’t have a strong hand. You can act last on the river and potentially bluff if a 5 or 9 comes, or fold if a non-helping card appears and they bet.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
